  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any market-exclusion or sales-stop consequence for a 5% failure rate, making it a review benchmark, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 makes recall discretionary rather than mandatory at 8 per 100,000, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), and S3's six-year retrofit window is compatible with Northwind's low shut-off coverage. S4's 36-month suppression deadline meets Halcyon's red line and S1 is reasonably strict on timing but limits reporting to confirmed incidents."
